{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106673","id":2534091892,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6XCyx0","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106673","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106673.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106673.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106673","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106673/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106673/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106673/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/ba06234309ee1b4510ad5251b9957853c572e24c","number":106673,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix light range in VoxelGI","user":{"login":"retrotails","id":10767978,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNzY3OTc4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10767978?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails","html_url":"https://github.com/retrotails","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I don't know what I'm doing here, I'd appreciate if someone more familiar with the code base could help me if there's a better way to do this.\r\n\r\nfixes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/80101\r\nthanks to @juniez3d in that thread for their comment that led me the right direction\r\n\r\nthis PR fixes a bug where voxel GI has the wrong radius for lights, because I think it internally uses voxels as units instead of godot units, and they aren't getting converted. this leads to bugs like changing the voxel resolution affecting light brightness, cartoony looking lights with a harsh edge because the radius that clips the light is properly calculated but not the attenuation, and incorrect light attenuation because attenuation works in world space (though that honestly seems like it's own bug...).\r\n\r\nthis might improve https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/55639 but probably isn't a fix since that scene uses a directional light which isn't helped by this PR.\r\n\r\n![pr](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/45844a8c-9ffe-4bfa-b261-d415bb146dc1)\r\ntop is 1.0 attenuation, bottom is ~8.0 attenuation, right 4 images are voxel debug view\r\n\r\n_bugsquad edit: fixes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107118_","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12070367,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AuC3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/mile